  "$comment": "The conformance FONT SET: every theme font family name → the font files BOTH renderers lay text out with (the web as @font-face rules named after the family, served from these files; gpui as the ONLY fonts in a cosmic-text system without system fonts). Paths are repo-relative and committed. A family without committed files names a `substitute` (its metrics are the substitute's, on both sides — the comparison stays apples to apples, it no longer tests that family). CSS generic names the themes use as a family (`ui-monospace`) are mapped too. `default` = the face the desktop gets for `.SystemUIFont` and every unmapped family. Round 2: Nunito and Fira Code (the playful theme's families, SIL OFL 1.1, licences beside the files in conformance/fonts/) are real faces now; Nunito's statics are instances of Google Fonts' variable Nunito[wght].ttf (fonttools varLib.instancer --update-name-table), Fira Code's are the v6.2 release's. Not shipped in the npm package.",
